ts illustrious cast of  aaa talent he-man will have his shouts  and war cries powered by chris wood of  supergirl and the vampire diaries fame  the biggest scat of the series however  is without a doubt mark hamill  in a truly inspired casting choice he  will be lending his incredible voice  talents to iconic villain skeletor  hamill may still be most well known for  playing luke skywalker in the star wars  franchise but he's almost as famous for  his stellar body of voice acting work  he has consistently performed an  animated version of the joker since the  90s  more recently he has been putting his  evil shriek to work as skektec the  scientist in the other big 80s nostalgia  revival series on netflix the dark  crystal age of resistance  so becoming skeletor is a perfect fit  for his style what can we say he's very  good at those unhinged evil cackles  the celebrity train doesn't stop there  as we continue down the long list of  eternia's friends and enemies  the cast includes sarah michelle gellar  as tila liam cunningham as man in arms  lena heady is evil lin diedrick bader is  king randor and trap jaw  alicia silverstone as queen marlena and  many more there's even a role for kevin  conroy the batman to hamilt's joker and  batman the animated series as merman  hello hello operator i believe my  party's been  disconnected  netflix's sparse webpage for the  upcoming masters of the universe  revelation series has a brief  one-sentence blurb as a summary of the  show  that reads after a calamitous battle  fractures eternia tila and an unlikely  alliance must prevent the end of the  universe and the sequel to the 80s  classic  exciting eh netflix's teaser doesn't  provide much more context than that but  by the power of greyskull it does feel  like a direct continuation of the 80  series complete with 95 seconds of  action set to bonnie tyler's holding out  for a hero  like so at the beginning of our first  episode it plays for the first 10  minutes  like you know 